  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Generally dry weather today through late next \nweek.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA strong surface high pressure will elongate across the\nnortheastern United States beginning today, and will generally \ncontrol the weather through late next week. A strong low- \npressure system in the central Atlantic stays well to our east \nMonday night through Thursday as a result. \n\nA weak cold front is expected to move through on Tuesday. \nHowever, with only limited moisture available, not anticipating \nrainfall with this. There is no clear signal for any \nprecipitation through at least next weekend as several high\npressure systems cross the region mid to late week. High temperatures\nare expected to be seasonable in the 50s mid week, cooling\ntowards the 40s through the end of the week.",
